---
import RaceLayout from '../layouts/RaceLayout.astro';
import Garage from '../components/garage/Garage.astro';
import ControlsTables from '../components/garage/ControlsTables.astro';
import StatusBadge from '../components/StatusBadge.astro';
import { BINDING, PAD_DEFAULT, PRESETS, SOURCE, STATUS, TESTED_CONTROLLERS, type Status } from '../lib/controls';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<RaceLayout
	title="Garage: ReCarbon controls"
	description="ReCarbon's keyboard and controller controls, interactive: driving, menus and the Settings overlay, with how each one was verified."
>
	<section class="section garage-page">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">Garage · Controls</p>
			<h1 class="display title chrome">Tune your controls</h1>
			<p class="intro">
				ReCarbon turns the keyboard into an Xbox 360 controller. Pick a device, a mode and a keyboard preset
				({PRESETS.map((p) => p.name).join(', ')}); hover, tap or tab through the list to light up each control. The Garage
				shows ReCarbon's <strong>built-in presets</strong> only: your own profiles are made in game.
			</p>

			<Garage />

			<div class="panels">
				<details class="panel cut">
					<summary>Text table: every mode</summary>
					<ControlsTables />
				</details>

				<details class="panel cut" id="your-bindings">
					<summary>Presets and your own profiles</summary>
					<p>
						ReCarbon has two built-in keyboard presets. <strong>WASD</strong>, what a new player starts with, is the original
						layout: it drives with W A S D, and the arrow keys work the left stick (Left and Right steer too) and the D-pad at
						once. <strong>Arrows</strong> drives with the arrows and leaves W A S D to the D-pad; in it no key does two things.
						The built-ins can't be changed.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Custom profiles are configured in game</strong>, not on this site. Open Settings (<kbd aria-label="Command">⌘</kbd> + <kbd>,</kbd>;
						or <kbd>F1</kbd> / <kbd>Fn</kbd> + <kbd>F1</kbd>) and go to <strong>Controls</strong> with <kbd>Q</kbd> /
						<kbd>E</kbd>: the <strong>Keyboard Profile</strong> row switches profiles at once. Rebinding a key of a built-in
						preset makes a copy of it, such as “WASD (custom)”. Controller buttons are rebound on the
						<strong>Controller</strong> tab, which has its own <strong>Controller Profile</strong> row.
					</p>
					<p>
						Profiles live in <code>~/Library/Application Support/ReCarbon/profiles/</code> (<code>keyboard.toml</code> and
						<code>controller.toml</code>). The active keyboard profile's keys are also written to the <code>[keys]</code>
						table of <code>settings.toml</code>, so an older ReCarbon still finds them.
						<a href={url('docs/controls/#presets-and-profiles')}>More on profiles</a>
					</p>
				</details>

				<details class="panel cut" id="controller-notes">
					<summary>Controller notes</summary>
					<ul class="proof">
						<li><StatusBadge status={BINDING.controller.status} /> The default mapping below is pinned by unit tests.</li>
						<li>
							<StatusBadge status={BINDING.virtualController.status} /> SDL's virtual controller drives the menus, survives
							unplugging, and rebinds buttons in Settings &gt; Controller. That is automated evidence, not a hardware test.
						</li>
						<li>
							<StatusBadge status={BINDING.physicalController.status} /> No physical controller has been hand-tested with ReCarbon
							yet, and controller rebinding hasn't been tried on hardware. What each button does in a race is known only from the keyboard and the virtual controller.
						</li>
					</ul>
					<h3 class="notes-h">Default controller profile</h3>
					<p>
						Pads are read through SDL3 <strong>by button position</strong>. The Xbox / PlayStation switch above changes the
						names shown, not this mapping. Triggers, sticks and their deadzones are fixed; only the buttons can be rebound,
						in game.
					</p>
					<div class="ctl-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Default controller profile">
						<table class="pad-default">
							<thead>
								<tr>
									<th scope="col">Xbox 360 control</th>
									<th scope="col">Pad button (position)</th>
									<th scope="col">PlayStation-style label</th>
								</tr>
							</thead>
							<tbody>
								{PAD_DEFAULT.map((b) => (
									<tr>
										<th scope="row">{b.control}</th>
										<td>{b.xbox}</td>
										<td>{b.ps}</td>
									</tr>
								))}
							</tbody>
						</table>
					</div>
					<ul>
						<li>
							<StatusBadge status="not-mapped" /> Back paddles, extra buttons and the Guide button aren't read by ReCarbon.
							If a pad's own firmware or software remaps a paddle to another button, it acts as that button: ReCarbon only
							sees the result.
						</li>
					</ul>
				</details>

				<section class="panel cut" aria-labelledby="tested-title">
					<h2 id="tested-title">Tested controllers</h2>
					{
						TESTED_CONTROLLERS.length ? (
							<ul>
								{TESTED_CONTROLLERS.map((t) => (
									<li>
										<strong>{t.model}</strong>: hand-tested {t.date}. {t.evidence}
									</li>
								))}
							</ul>
						) : (
							<p>
								None yet: the physical controller test is deferred. A controller model is listed here only after it passes a
								physical hand test with ReCarbon; virtual-controller runs don't count. A listing records a test result; it is
								not an endorsement or a recommendation.
							</p>
						)
					}
				</section>

				<section class="panel cut legend" aria-labelledby="legend-title">
					<h2 id="legend-title">Status legend</h2>
					<ul>
						{
							(Object.keys(STATUS) as Status[]).map((s) => (
								<li>
									<StatusBadge status={s} /> <span>{STATUS[s].meaning}</span>
								</li>
							))
						}
					</ul>
					<p class="src">
						Generated from ReCarbon's source{SOURCE.commit && <> at <code>{SOURCE.commit.slice(0, 7)}</code></>}:
						{SOURCE.files.map((f, i) => (
							<>
								{i > 0 && ', '}
								<code>{f}</code>
							</>
						))}.
					</p>
				</section>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</RaceLayout>

<style>
	.title {
		font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 4rem);
	}
	.intro {
		max-width: 44rem;
		margin: 1rem 0 2rem;
		color: var(--text-2);
	}
	.panels {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
	}
	.panel {
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		background: var(--surface);
		border: 1px solid var(--line);
	}
	.panel summary {
		min-height: 44px;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		font-family: var(--rn-font-display);
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	.panel h2 {
		margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
		font-family: var(--rn-font-display);
		font-size: 1rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}
	.panel :global(kbd) {
		font-family: var(--rn-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.8em;
		padding: 0 0.35em;
		border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
		border-bottom-width: 2px;
		border-radius: 3px;
	}
	.panel h3.notes-h {
		margin: 1.25rem 0 0.5rem;
		font-family: var(--rn-font-display);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}
	.proof {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.4rem;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}
	.ctl-scroll {
		overflow-x: auto;
	}
	.pad-default {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 36rem;
		border-collapse: collapse;
		font-size: 0.875rem;
	}
	.pad-default :is(th, td) {
		padding: 0.35rem 0.6rem;
		text-align: start;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
	}
	.pad-default thead th {
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}
	.panel pre {
		overflow-x: auto;
		padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
		background: var(--page-bg);
		border: 1px solid var(--line);
		font-family: var(--rn-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}
	.panel code {
		font-family: var(--rn-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.85em;
		overflow-wrap: anywhere;
	}
	.legend ul {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}
	.legend li {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 9.5rem 1fr;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		align-items: baseline;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}
	.src {
		margin: 1rem 0 0;
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}
</style>
